{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "papers": [
    {
      "id": "8c8e315d-55c9-4262-8a6d-b884ad2e06cb",
      "title": "From Components to Instances: Iterative Composition",
      "templateRef": {
        "id": "exploration",
        "version": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "ada40061-3d12-4cf3-ba56-bda67cd92f32",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Abstract",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "04e3813b-316e-4224-b7af-72e2fc009553",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Working proposal only. This paper investigates whether repeated, constraint-guided composition can grow existing components into an intent-specific instance. No experimental findings are claimed.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "4fe87295-e058-485f-9626-c1a63d54171e",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Introduction and Research Question",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "e2d035ce-994b-4365-a454-d56bc6056911",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Can an iterative algorithm use the available components’ capabilities, interfaces, dependencies, and constraints to propose composites, represent viable assemblies at higher planes, and continue until a specified instance intent is satisfied? The user describes this as System 1 thinking guided by the components’ genetic makeup. These are working metaphors whose technical meanings remain to be defined.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "f5070b19-7e66-4932-8af6-3d54f1dacd0a",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Background and Related Work",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "f308ddef-6d69-48e1-b929-6765801fd956",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Not researched yet.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "46948b81-56ec-47c0-8a3b-ca4293070159",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Provisional Hypotheses and Predictions",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "bedf4cf3-f48d-4776-b707-df7495c8d322",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Proposed hypothesis: capability-guided candidate selection, explicit compatibility checks, and feedback from validation can produce increasingly useful assemblies while reusing previously validated pieces. This hypothesis is untested.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "eb96be4c-fb2b-4e88-8ba1-95814cdfddfd",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Assumptions and Alternative Explanations",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "b89d37d1-b5a1-489b-8a8a-1dd994f2fc7e",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Open assumptions: component descriptions contain enough information to judge useful combinations; local compatibility can be supplemented by assembly-level behavior checks; repeated composition improves requirement coverage rather than merely adding layers. Compare against predefined recipes and unguided composition.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "d40c0619-0e66-485f-b47a-27ea5438e60f",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Methods of Inquiry",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "6ab1d49a-253c-49bf-95eb-e3ed9a09862e",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Proposed loop for discussion: identify an unresolved requirement; inspect available pieces; propose a candidate assembly; validate its interfaces and behavior; reject or revise failures; expose a successful assembly as a reusable higher-layer item; reassess the remaining requirements. Define evaluation tasks, baselines, budgets, and stopping rules before testing.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "8e545baf-875b-485e-9f1c-f780141e8b87",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Results and Evidence",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "b5b52918-7992-44c9-bf49-6badf8c7e0a4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No experiment has been run for this research question. Existing canvas demonstrations do not establish that this general algorithm works.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "0ce3f7a2-520b-4f24-a193-0da1cb0f829d",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Discussion and Critical Evaluation",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "e0661f09-ccb9-477a-a411-4f34aa3e43ae",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "To be developed after defining the mechanism and collecting evidence.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "ee5827db-743f-4b46-80df-d20214e137d5",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Limitations and Validity",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "f23e893d-590d-41ca-93f9-6bd4a61f38dc",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Compatibility alone does not establish usefulness or correctness. More abstraction layers do not necessarily indicate progress. Hidden dependencies, inaccurate capability descriptions, and failed assumptions may prevent a viable assembly.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "8d35bc6d-a55d-4b8b-b2b7-e8c12554ceea",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Conclusion",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "0cd10e49-4b09-4dc9-9821-00f73889a1b6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Unresolved. This is a research direction, not an established capability.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "2ea55d7d-2cfa-4306-8a60-d87ffbab064e",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Open Questions and Next Tests",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "eab0f5c9-b8cd-444e-aa7f-e63d89912392",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What precisely does System 1 mean here: rapid retrieval of known assemblies, learned candidate ranking, or another mechanism? What constitutes the genetic makeup of a component? What measurable requirement coverage, validation evidence, and resource limits define a substantial instance and stop the iteration?",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "60c54de4-5b86-44f0-8644-85c65ede59da",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Reproducibility and Disclosures",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "c2304466-f48b-4921-ab2f-800dbc920593",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Initial idea supplied by the user; organization and provisional wording assisted by AI. No external literature review or experimental evaluation has yet been performed.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "f8ec819c-ff6b-42d9-9471-dfb4071fded3",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
